From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Noronha Silva <gustavo@noronha.dev.br>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 22:19:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] virgl: do not offer three-plane 4:2:0 as a decode
 target

virgl_is_video_format_supported deferred wholesale to the generic helper, which answers a
different question than the one asked -- its own comment is "we at least need to sample
from it". Every 4:2:0 layout decomposes to R8, so NV12, YV12 and IYUV were all advertised
for decode. Every other driver implementing this hook answers from real decode caps
instead (radeonsi, si_vid_is_format_supported).

The surplus is not harmless. ffmpeg picks a surface format by exact match against
sw_pix_fmt -- get_pix_fmt_score short-circuits to INT_MAX when dst == src -- so for an
8-bit 4:2:0 stream I420 and YV12 both outscore NV12, and the last advertised wins. Firefox
refuses the I420 surface it is then handed, tears down its frame pool and decodes in
software. Hardware decode is advertised, selected, and silently never used; measured
guest-side as three processes at ~20%% CPU with libdav1d in perf top, on a host that was
decoding nothing.

Withholding the two planar layouts from decode targets leaves NV12, which is what VA-API
decoders emit. Encode and video processing are untouched, as is every other format.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
index aabb7ad44e2..d2b6de7b80b 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
@@ -775,7 +775,28 @@ static bool virgl_is_video_format_supported(struct pipe_screen *screen,
                                             enum pipe_video_profile profile,
                                             enum pipe_video_entrypoint entrypoint)
 {
-    return vl_video_buffer_is_format_supported(screen, format, profile, entrypoint);
+   /* A decoder does not produce three-plane 4:2:0. The generic helper answers a
+    * different question than the one asked -- its own comment is "we at least need to
+    * sample from it" -- so it accepts NV12, YV12 and IYUV alike, all of which decompose
+    * to R8 and so all of which the screen can sample. Every other driver implementing
+    * this hook answers from real decode caps instead (radeonsi, si_vid_is_format_supported);
+    * virgl deferred wholesale.
+    *
+    * The result is not a harmless surplus. ffmpeg chooses a surface format by exact match
+    * against sw_pix_fmt (vaapi_decode_find_best_format, and get_pix_fmt_score short-circuits
+    * to INT_MAX when dst == src), so for an 8-bit 4:2:0 stream I420 and YV12 both outscore
+    * NV12 and the last one advertised wins. Firefox then refuses the surface it is handed,
+    * tears down its frame pool and decodes in software: hardware decode is advertised,
+    * selected, and silently never used.
+    *
+    * So the two planar 4:2:0 layouts are withheld from decode targets, leaving NV12 -- what
+    * VA-API decoders actually emit. Encode and video processing are untouched, and so is
+    * every other format. */
+   if (entrypoint == PIPE_VIDEO_ENTRYPOINT_BITSTREAM &&
+       (format == PIPE_FORMAT_YV12 || format == PIPE_FORMAT_IYUV))
+      return false;
+
+   return vl_video_buffer_is_format_supported(screen, format, profile, entrypoint);
 }
 
 
